        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikhail Glinka, Jean-Baptiste Lully\n- Roles: Composer, instrumentalist, dancer\n- Places: Russia, France\n- Concepts: Russian classical music, court of Louis XIV\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully was born as Giovanni Battista Lulli on 28 November 1632 and died on 22 March 1687.\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully was an Italian-born French composer, instrumentalist, and dancer who spent most of his life working at the court of Louis XIV of France.\n- Mikhail Ivanovich Glinka was born on 1 June 1804 and died on 15 February 1857.\n- Mikhail Glinka was the first Russian composer to gain wide recognition within Russia and is often regarded as the fountainhead of Russian classical music.",
